1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,103
Two students are preparing for the gaokao.

2
00:00:03,103 --> 00:00:05,784
One of them also sits a university interview.

3
00:00:06,104 --> 00:00:08,600
So what does that interview actually give them?

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:10,925
This is comprehensive evaluation:

5
00:00:10,925 --> 00:00:14,509
the university adds its own assessment to the gaokao score.

6
00:00:14,829 --> 00:00:18,219
Take XJTLU's 2026 rules for Jiangsu:

7
00:00:18,219 --> 00:00:21,421
the composite score is out of 100.

8
00:00:21,741 --> 00:00:26,052
The gaokao, scaled to 100 points, counts for 65 percent.

9
00:00:26,052 --> 00:00:28,824
The interview counts for 35 percent.

10
00:00:29,144 --> 00:00:34,135
Student A scores 600 on the gaokao and 90 in the interview.

11
00:00:34,135 --> 00:00:36,504
Student B scores 615 and 70.

12
00:00:36,824 --> 00:00:44,397
Scaling the gaokao from 750, A gets 83.50, and B gets 77.80.

13
00:00:44,717 --> 00:00:46,824
Fifteen points behind on the gaokao,

14
00:00:46,824 --> 00:00:48,813
and the interview turns it around.

15
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:51,622
That's the first thing it adds:

16
00:00:51,622 --> 00:00:54,456
points you can earn by preparing, beyond the gaokao.

17
00:00:54,776 --> 00:00:57,634
You must still clear the special-category control line,

18
00:00:57,634 --> 00:00:59,661
and a weak interview can pull you back.

19
00:00:59,981 --> 00:01:02,520
The second thing is one more chance to be admitted.

20
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:07,277
XJTLU says you can still apply in the regular undergraduate round.

21
00:01:07,597 --> 00:01:10,776
CUHK-Shenzhen says it doesn't affect your later applications.

22
00:01:11,096 --> 00:01:14,189
But move to another province, and the rules can change.

23
00:01:14,509 --> 00:01:17,268
In Guangdong, it's 65 percent gaokao,

24
00:01:17,268 --> 00:01:21,741
30 interview and 5 academic tests, with a May 20th deadline.

25
00:01:22,061 --> 00:01:25,581
So always check which province and which year the rules are for.

26
00:01:25,901 --> 00:01:28,555
It takes time, too: apply in April or May,

27
00:01:28,555 --> 00:01:30,829
and interview soon after the gaokao.

28
00:01:31,149 --> 00:01:34,382
The interview? The brochure says it assesses English,

29
00:01:34,382 --> 00:01:37,677
overall competence and ability, not subject knowledge.

30
00:01:37,997 --> 00:01:38,644
In practice,

31
00:01:38,644 --> 00:01:41,773
that means stating a view and a reason clearly in English.

32
00:01:42,093 --> 00:01:43,370
Write only an opinion,

33
00:01:43,370 --> 00:01:46,561
and the feedback flags the missing reason. Add because,

34
00:01:46,561 --> 00:01:47,490
and check again.

35
00:01:50,410 --> 00:01:53,860
So it adds one more assessment and one more admission chance,

36
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:56,575
at the cost of thresholds, time and preparation.

37
00:01:56,895 --> 00:01:59,467
Before applying, check three things: your province,

38
00:01:59,467 --> 00:02:00,981
whether you'll clear the line,

39
00:02:00,981 --> 00:02:02,847
and whether you have time to prepare.
